{
  "id": "Compound::DB00349 - Gene::6529",
  "verbalization": "Clobazam exhibits a strong binding interaction with Slc6a11, a splice variant of the Slc6a1 gene. This binding is linked to the participation of Slc6a11 in Gamma-aminobutyric acid (GABA) sodium symporter activity and GABA transmembrane transporter activity. These activities are critical for the transport of GABA across cellular membranes, a process essential for neurotransmission. The evidence suggests that Clobazam may modulate the function of Slc6a11, potentially influencing GABA transport and thereby affecting neuronal signaling. The consistent scores across both paths indicate a robust, biologically relevant interaction, though the exact mechanism of how Clobazam alters Slc6a11 function remains to be fully elucidated. The relationship is supported by a clear, ontological pathway that connects Clobazam to Slc6a11 through its role in regulating GABA transport.",
